{title: What a Friend We Have in Jesus}
{artist: Joseph M. Scriven (1819-1886)}
{key: F}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[F]What a friend we have in Jesus, [Bb]all our sins and griefs to [F]bear!
[F]What a privilege to [Dm]carry [C]everything to God in [F]prayer!
[C]O what peace we often [F]forfeit, [Bb]O what needless pain we [C]bear,
[F]All because we do not [Bb]carry [C]everything to God in [F]prayer.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[F]Have we trials and temp[Bb]tations? Is there trouble any[F]where?
[F]We should never be dis[Dm]couraged; [C]take it to the Lord in [F]prayer.
[C]Can we find a friend so [F]faithful [Bb]who will all our sorrows [C]share?
[F]Jesus knows our every [Bb]weakness; [C]take it to the Lord in [F]prayer.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[F]Are we weak and heavy [Bb]laden, cumbered with a load of [F]care?
[F]Precious Savior, still our [Dm]refuge— [C]take it to the Lord in [F]prayer.
[C]Do thy friends despise, for[F]sake thee? [Bb]Take it to the Lord in [C]prayer;
[F]In His arms He’ll take and [Bb]shield thee; [C]thou wilt find a solace [F]there.
{eov}
